g/freedesktop/DBus: unknown error type: \n[2147:2172:1013/043621.181846:ERROR:dbus/bus.cc:405] Failed to connect to the bus: Could not parse server address: Unknown address type (examples of valid types are \"tcp\" and on UNIX \"unix\")\n[2147:2147:1013/043621.456579:ERROR:dbus/object_proxy.cc:572] Failed to call method: org.freedesktop.DBus.NameHasOwner: object_path= /org/freedesktop/DBus: unknown error type: \n[2147:2173:1013/043625.474503:ERROR:google_apis/gcm/engine/registration_request.cc:291] Registration response error message: DEPRECATED_ENDPOINT\nCreated TensorFlow Lite XNNPACK delegate for CPU.\n","lastPage":{"url":"http://127.0.0.1:33471/","focus":"<button id=\"openWeek\" type=\"button\">Open saved week</button>","text":"TasteTable\n\nA weekly plan of restaurants + one cultural outing, grounded in Qloo taste data and checked against care constraints.\n\nNot medical or dietary advice. Constraint checks are heuristics over public venue tags and menu keywords. Always confirm accessibility, texture and sodium needs with the venue and the person's care team. Sample personas are fictional; do not enter real health information.\n1. Tastes & constraints\nOpen saved week\nCompare saved weeks (new tab)\nVisit record (new tab)\nTry a sample persona\nFavourite cuisines \nMusic they love (artists / era) \nFavourite films \nCity \nConstraints\n Soft foods  Low sodium  Wheelchair access\nPlan my week\n\nKeep your caregiver handoff\n\nSave the arranged week and all its venue notes in one editable file. Open a handoff to review it before replacing the current week and notes.\n\nSave caregiver handoff (.json)\nOpen caregiver handoff\n\nKeep the file to continue later. Files are read locally; nothing is saved automatically or sent to a provider. Original checks are retained without being run again.\n\nSaved in this browser\n\nKeep named planning drafts in this browser. Each explicit Save keeps the original inputs, source evidence and arranged dates. Venue call notes are not included. It is not refreshed automatically. Clearing this site's browser data removes these drafts.\n\nRefresh saved weeks\n\nMIT licensed · Uses Qloo's Taste AI insights. Qloo results describe aggregate affinities, not facts about any individual."},"pageErrors":[],"nativeFileChooserEvents":0,"totalArtifactBytes":130165}
